      'Tom Segura is coming to The Buddy Holly Hall. The venue presale starts April 2, 2025, at 10 AM with the code: TOGETHER. ABOUT TOM SEGURA: Actor, comedian, and writer Tom Segura is one of the biggest names in comedy today. He is currently selling out venues worldwide on his Come Together tour, following his highly successful I’m Coming Everywhere World Tour, where he performed over 300 shows. Segura is best known for his Netflix specials Ball Hog (2020), Disgraceful (2018), Mostly Stories (2016), and Completely Normal (2014). His fifth Netflix special, Sledgehammer, was released on July 4, 2023, and debuted at #1 on the platform. Segura will next be seen starring in the upcoming dark comedy series Bad Thoughts, premiering on Netflix on May 13th, which he produced through YMH Studios. In July 2022, Segura released his New York Times bestselling book I’d Like to Play Alone, Please, widely praised with Forbes calling it “laugh out loud funny.” Paste Magazine described him as having a natural storytelling ability that lifts his narratives beyond average anecdotes into hilarious territory. Your Mom’s House Studios, which he co-hosts with his wife, comedian Christina Pazsitzky, is home to hit podcasts like Your Mom’s House and 2 Bears 1 Cave (co-hosted with Bert Kreischer), drawing millions of weekly listeners. YMH Studios also pioneered successful livestream podcast events during the pandemic. Segura’s film credits include STX Film Countdown opposite Elizabeth Lail, Instant Family opposite Mark Wahlberg and Rose Byrne, OPENING ACT, and FLINCH. His television appearances include The Late Show with Stephen Colbert, Conan, Workaholics, Happy Endings, The Late Late Show, Comedy Central Presents: Tom Segura, Mash Up, and How To Be A Grown Up. With an increasing social media following (@seguratom on Instagram and @tomsegura on Twitter), when not performing or podcasting, Segura enjoys watching college football or eagerly awaiting its return.',
